sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-model-fidelity> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Mitchison (1980, 1981) & Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) with-the-flux auxin canalization: exponent bifurcation, growing hex-lamina canalization (solved), Sachs wound bypass (solved + prescribed), hand-drawn Feugier venation templates, and cleared-leaf specimen segmentation — Model fidelity to source: 72/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Credited: `HexCanalizationLattice.step` (L808-828) integrates the seed paper's Eq. 2-3 pair (dS = sigma - mu S - sum D (S_i - S_j); dD = alpha |phi|^p/(1 + (|phi|/phi_s)^p) + beta - gamma D) with a semi-implicit S update, wall re-symmetrisation and a documented saturation; `refine_hex_lattice` (L881-913) implements cell division with conductance inheritance; Law 2 drainage now EMERGES (0.67 < 1) instead of being written in; the saturation law is machine-checked in Lean (bounded + monotone). The Sachs incision is solved on the same engine with blocked walls (L1064-1075) and an alpha = 0 control. Deductions: the remediation item asked for polar PIN1 carrier allocation on a growing mesh and the shipped model is facilitated diffusion on a hex lattice (-6); `simulate_2d_lamina_canalization` (L243-335) and the 12-column profiles in `simulate_mitchison_exponent_sweep` (L170-198) are analytic constructions with hard-coded dip ratios 0.3105 / 0.6895 (L195, L295), and the p = 1.4 point uses a special-cased eff_beta = 0.1766 (L158) so the sweep is partly fitted to its own reference (-8); `simulate_sachs_wound_bypass` (L338-414) is a Gaussian centreline plus the constants 0.9852 / 0.0804 (L408-409), still returned and plotted (-4); `simulate_feugier_venation_topologies` (L446-548) solves nothing - V/E/C are typed in (L493, L523) - so Law 3 has no dynamical realisation (-6); the solved growing lamina yields a basal fan of lattice-aligned strands (two stage-1 strands plus parallel secondaries, Panel C of the growing-lamina PNG) rather than a pinnate midrib, and no parameter study shows that the hexagonal anisotropy is not driving it (-4)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py L243–L335: simulate_2d_lamina_canalization writes D and S as Gaussian formulas; drainage fraction 0.6895 (L295) is a constant chosen to hit the 0.31 reference - not a solution of the model <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L243-L335>",
            "1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py L446–L548: simulate_feugier_venation_topologies hand-draws two graphs; V_open/E_open (L493) and V_closed/E_closed (L523) are literals, no carrier dynamics are integrated <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L446-L548>" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-model-fidelity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-model-fidelity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-model-fidelity-3> ;
        pk:hasScore "0.72"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-model-fidelity-1> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py L736–L879" ;
        dct:description "HexCanalizationLattice: Mitchison (1980) Eqs. 2-3 solved on a hex lattice; semi-implicit S (L816), saturating feedback (L820), optional irreversibility (L824), enclosed-region (Betti-1) counter (L854-878)" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L736-L879> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-model-fidelity-2> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py L881–L1034" ;
        dct:description "refine_hex_lattice cell-division inheritance (same-parent walls take max of the parent's two wall conductances, L902-905) and simulate_growing_lamina_venation 3-stage driver with nesting / Betti-1 / angle / mass-balance records (L990-1020)" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L881-L1034> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-model-fidelity-3> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_034_auxin_canalization_leaf_veins.lean L120–L178" ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 theorems saturating_canalization_feedback_bounded (L131-146), saturating_canalization_feedback_monotone (L148-167), irreversible_differentiation_monotone (L176-178); lean exits 0, 0 sorrys" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_034_auxin_canalization_leaf_veins.lean#L120-L178> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (MorphoEval Autonomous Loop Slot 034 Pass 3 Assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

